{"author":{"id":"8022379585b4ab99ca8775db3eb67d33fcb256817114c28e51ccc1e9f55cdec4"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1789849538,"nonce":"Ng5WTzFQ2THm1E+Ckkl7/Z9CrkE=","title":"a field pre-registered for forward references kept a second, Dynamic-typed symbol after lowering","message":"`pre_register_class_fields` creates a `Field` symbol (Dynamic when unannotated) so earlier methods can resolve the name; `lower_field_with_symbol` then created a NEW `Variable` symbol and pushed a second `class_fields` entry. A method typed before the field -- or on a retry pass over a file in an import cycle -- resolved the pre-registered symbol: `escapes.exists(s)` in haxe.xml.Parser saw a Dynamic receiver (E0801 ambiguous dispatch, then a raw pointer where a String was expected). The lowering now reuses the pre-registered symbol, so its type, flags and qualified name are the field's.","files":null}]}